    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Seljalandsfoss + Gljúfrabúi</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>08:30–09:45</b><br><br>You wake up next to it — beat the tour buses. Walk behind the falls (raincoats); Gljúfrabúi is 600 m up the path.<br><br>◈ The famous one — behind the curtain looking out through the water — is a sunset picture, and you are here at 08:30. Take the empty path instead; no light beats having nobody else in the frame. The sun is low behind the falls from the front, so expect a rainbow in the spray. At <b>Gljúfrabúi</b> the picture is the shaft of daylight down the cleft.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop3</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-19.9886,63.6156</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Skógafoss + Kvernufoss</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>10:15–11:45</b><br><br>The banked half-hour means Kvernufoss fits — 20-min walk from the museum lot, most people miss it.<br><br>◈ Skógafoss faces <b>south</b> and you are here with the sun in the south-east — front-lit, which is precisely when its rainbow shows. Take it low from the river stones first, then climb the 527 steps for the one looking back down the escarpment.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop3</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-19.5114,63.5321</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Katla ice cave</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>14:00–17:00</b> · <i>booked</i><br><br>Troll Expeditions, ticket TRO-T141847549 (order TRO-100452964) — 3 adult tickets, paid in full. Lunch in Vík 12:15 (Smiðjan Brugghús), then meet in the Víkinn Hotel lobby in Vík — check in by 13:40, 20 min before the 14:00 departure, and look for the super jeeps marked Troll Expeditions. Complimentary coffee and cookies in the lobby if you're early. Super-jeep up onto Mýrdalsjökull to blue glacier ice; 17:00 is an estimate — the ticket states no duration. Jeans are not allowed on the glacier: waterproof shell, thermal base layer, hat and gloves. Boots and waterproofs rent on site, all sizes — tell the guide if you pre-booked extras. Free to cancel until 24 hrs before, nothing back inside that. Check road.is and your email (inbox and spam) before setting off; weather cancellations go out by email.<br><br>◈ Put a person in the frame or nothing shows the scale. Phones handle blue ice better than you would expect; keep your headlamp out of other people's shots.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop3</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-18.88,63.6</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Dyrhólaey</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>17:15–18:00</b><br><br>The rock arch and the best coastal panorama in the south.<br><br>◈ From the top, looking east along the whole black curve to the Reynisdrangar stacks. Sun at 13° in the west-south-west, so the sand is lit warm and the arch reads as a silhouette.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop3</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-19.1306,63.4022</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Reynisfjara</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>18:10–19:00</b><br><br>Golden-hour basalt. Sneaker waves: obey the warning lights, stay off the wet sand. Farmhouse is 15 min back west — dinner in Vík first, or groceries at Krónan.<br><br>◈ The best forty minutes of light on the trip. Sun at <b>7° in the west-south-west</b> rakes along the basalt columns and makes the hexagons glow, and the stacks to the east are front-lit. Eyes on the water the whole time — no photograph here is worth standing on wet sand.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop3</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-19.0446,63.4043</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Lava Show, Vík</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>~20:00</b> · <i>optional</i><br><br>Real molten lava indoors — if there's gas left in the tank.<br><br>◈ Real molten lava a few feet away in a dark room. Flash off — the glow is the picture.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop3</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-19.006,63.4187</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Night 3 · Mýrdalur (near Dyrhólaey)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Farmhouse Lodge (Airbnb)</b><br>Skeiðflöt, 871 Mýrdalur — 10 min from Dyrhólaey, 15 min west of Vík]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#base3</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-19.19,63.4375</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
  </Folder>
