    <Placemark>
      <name>Stokksnes / Vestrahorn</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>08:50–10:00</b><br><br>Morning light on the black dunes; small access fee at the Viking Café.<br><br>◈ The iconic Iceland frame: <b>Vestrahorn</b>'s teeth reflected in wet black sand with dune grass in front. The mountain is north-west of you and the sun is at 12° in the east-south-east over your shoulder, so the peak is fully lit — morning is the only time this works. It needs wet flats, so it wants a low or falling tide. The strip below fills in the day's low water once the marine forecast reaches this date, about two weeks out — it is a model rather than the Icelandic harbour table, so trust the timing and not the heights, and the reference station if you want to check is Hornafjörður.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop5</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-14.98,64.2434</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Djúpivogur</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>11:05–11:45</b><br><br>Eggin í Gleðivík egg sculptures + coffee.<br><br>◈ The row of granite eggs receding along the harbour rail — shoot down the line, never across it.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop5</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-14.2846,64.6562</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Petra&apos;s Stone Collection</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>12:45–13:45</b> · <i>optional</i><br><br>Quirky, kid-friendly and genuinely on the coastal road — which is the catch. Route 1 cuts inland to Egilsstaðir, so taking Petra's commits you to the full fjord coast: <b>+68 km</b>, the biggest optional detour on the trip and more than Seyðisfjörður costs. Packed lunch here.<br><br>◈ Close-ups, not wide shots: spar, jasper and zeolites by the thousand. Let the kid pick the subject.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop5</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-13.877,64.836</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Seyðisfjörður or Vök Baths</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>15:30–18:00</b> · <i>optional</i><br><br>Pick one afternoon: the rainbow-street town over the pass, or floating lake baths near Egilsstaðir. Seyðisfjörður is <b>+53 km</b> round trip over Fjarðarheiði; Vök is on the doorstep of tonight's base, so it costs nothing.<br><br>◈ If it is Seyðisfjörður, the <b>rainbow path</b> leading up to the blue church — the sister shot to day 1's street. If it is Vök, the pools cut into the lake surface with the swim-up bar in frame.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop5</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-14.01,65.261</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Night 5 · Egilsstaðir</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Eyjólfsstaðir Guesthouse</b><br>Eyjólfsstaðir, 701 Egilsstaðir — ~10 km southwest of town]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#base5</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-14.3945,65.2637</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
  </Folder>
