    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Stykkishólmur</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>08:30–09:30</b><br><br>Harbor, Súgandisey lighthouse hill, Danish-era houses — ten minutes north of the hotel, and first because you slept beside it. The old plan drove out to Kirkjufell and came back for this; sleeping here deletes that backtrack.<br><br>◈ Up on Súgandisey, the orange lighthouse against the fjord — and at 08:30 the sun is at <b>6°</b>, which is as good as light gets anywhere on this trip. The harbour and the Danish-era houses come free on the way back down.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop9</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-22.7297,65.0757</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Kirkjufell + Kirkjufellsfoss</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>10:10–10:55</b><br><br>The mountain everyone photographs, and the falls in front of it.<br><br>◈ The most photographed frame in Iceland, and genuinely worth it: <b>Kirkjufellsfoss</b> in the foreground, the mountain behind. Stand north-east of the falls looking north-west — the sun at 15° in the south-east is behind you, so the peak is lit rather than a shape.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop9</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-23.3068,64.942</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Djúpalónssandur</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>12:30–13:15</b><br><br>Lunch stop in Ólafsvík 11:40–12:10 en route. Pebble beach, lifting stones, wreck iron — same ocean caution as Reynisfjara.<br><br>◈ The rusted ribs of the trawler on black pebbles, taken low and close so the iron is huge and the beach is only backdrop. The lifting stones are the second frame, with a hand on one for scale.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop9</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-23.9033,64.7527</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Vatnshellir lava cave</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>13:20–14:05</b> · <i>optional</i><br><br>45-min guided cave, tours on the hour, kid-friendly.<br><br>◈ Almost nothing works down there — pitch dark, and the guide's lamp is the only light. Shoot the spiral staircase looking back up at the entrance hole instead; that one frame is the cave.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop9</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-23.818,64.748</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Arnarstapi · Gatklettur</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>14:15–15:10</b><br><br>Stone arch plus a stretch of the clifftop walk toward Hellnar.<br><br>◈ Gatklettur becomes a near-perfect circle when you find the angle — keep walking until the sea fills the hole. The kittiwake cliffs and the basalt columns are on the same short walk.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop9</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-23.6216,64.7686</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Búðakirkja</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>15:20–15:45</b><br><br>The black church in the lava field.<br><br>◈ The black church wants a low, wide frame with lava in front and mountains behind; it is small, and head-on makes it look smaller. Sun at 20° in the south-south-west lights the door side.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop9</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-23.3843,64.8221</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Ytri-Tunga seal beach</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>16:00–16:40</b><br><br>Seals haul out most days; then ~1 hr 30 inland to Reykholt, passing Borgarnes on the way.<br><br>◈ Longest lens you have, from where you already are. The picture is seals ignoring you — walking closer ends the scene, and is not allowed anyway.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop9</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-23.0784,64.8037</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Night 9 · Reykholt</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Fosshotel Reykholt</b><br>Reykholt, 320 Reykholt — inland on Route 518, 25 min short of Húsafell]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#base9</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-21.291,64.6652</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
  </Folder>
  <Folder>
    <name>Day 10–11 · Sep 28–29 · Into the Glacier · lava falls · hot spring, then home</name>
    <description><![CDATA[~200 km · out 08:45 · in 18:15]]></description>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Day 10 leg</name>
      <description><![CDATA[~200 km · 200.2 km by road, about 3.2 hrs driving]]></description>
