    <Placemark>
      <name>Leave Hotel Kríunes</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>08:15</b><br><br>Breakfast first, and ask the night before whether the partner rate includes it — the booking never spelled that out. The last night is at Elliðavatn rather than the airport, so the morning drives back out to Reykjanes on purpose: the peninsula's tip is the one corner of Iceland this trip never reaches otherwise.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop11</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-21.7938,64.0886</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Bridge Between Continents</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>09:10</b><br><br>The footbridge over the rift between the North American and Eurasian plates — ten minutes, and a good photograph for an 11-year-old who has just spent ten days on top of the seam.<br><br>◈ Stand in the rift and shoot along it with the bridge overhead. At 09:10 the sun is 9° up and throws a long shadow down the sand, which is the only thing that makes a shallow trench look like a plate boundary.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop11</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-22.675,63.868</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Gunnuhver</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>09:40</b><br><br>The boiling mud field, walked on boardwalks.<br><br>◈ The big vent throws a plume worth shooting into, with the low east-south-east sun behind it. Boardwalks only: the crust is thin and the ground is actually boiling.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop11</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-22.6836,63.8188</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Reykjanesviti + Valahnúkamöl</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>10:10</b><br><br>Iceland's oldest lighthouse on the cliff, and the sea stacks below it.<br><br>◈ Two frames — the lighthouse alone on its mound, and <b>Karl</b>, the sea stack, from the shore below with the surf breaking round it.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop11</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-22.7075,63.8125</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Brimketill</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>11:00</b><br><br>The lava rock pool the surf fills and empties. Watch it from the platform — people have been swept off these rocks.<br><br>◈ Wait for a set. The picture is the instant the surf pours over the lip and fills the pool; between waves it is just a rock. From the platform — people have been swept off trying for better.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop11</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-22.5122,63.8331</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Kaffi Duus — lunch</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>11:45</b><br><br>Fish on Keflavík harbour, ten minutes from the airport. If you want one last proper coffee, this is where it is: past security the airport side is chain-only.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop11</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-22.5636,64.0033</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>KEF terminal</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>14:40</b><br><br>Bag drop opens ~14:10; 1 carry-on (22 lbs) + 1 checked (50 lbs) each. KEF 17:10 → BOS → ATL 00:12.]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#stop11</styleUrl>
      <Point><coordinates>-22.605,63.985</coordinates></Point>
    </Placemark>
